            <ArticleTitle>Head and neck symptoms. Is the problem in the ears, face, neck, or oral cavity?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-7, 80, 83-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a complex anatomic and physiologic relationship among head and neck structures. Because of this complexity, patients with problems in any of these structures often present with a wide range of symptoms and physical findings. The authors describe many head and neck conditions that are encountered in a busy practice and emphasize selection of diagnostic studies and appropriate referral for treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
